  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># of Beneficiaries received employment/self-employment support.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP achieved significant success in advancing economic recovery and growth by reviving 80 workshops and providing in-demand vocational training and placement support to 253 beneficiaries. To further build on this success and enhance the impact of JP, UNDP will establish a referral mechanism to link JP-supported MSME owners and employment support beneficiaries, creating a mutually beneficial partnership between the business community and individuals seeking skilling and employment opportunities.
The referral mechanism creates a win-win situation for both MSMEs and employment support beneficiaries by facilitating direct job placements for VT beneficiaries in JP-supported MSMEs, fostering practical work-based experience, generating income opportunities, and local business recovery. Additionally, MSMEs can leverage the expertise of VT beneficiaries by enhancing their productivity and competitiveness. The initiative connects VT beneficiaries with MSMEs, creates job opportunity, promoting new business collaborations and integrating long-term economic development with skill development and livelihoods support. Furthermore Potential VT graduates might explore self-employment options through entrepreneurship and start-up support when possess a marketable idea that are responding to local needs.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="235" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="80"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># of MSMEs established/revived.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">To ensure economic growth and sustainability, UNDP&apos;s sustainability intervention builds upon the success of Phase I. Small grants provided to local businesses in Phase I successfully revitalized struggling enterprises, generated new jobs, and promoted industrial recovery. Nonetheless, challenges persist for MSMEs, including inadequate infrastructure and a shortage of essential skills and expertise necessary for a robust industrial economy. UNDP&apos;s sustainability intervention will tackle these challenges by rejuvenating specialized workshops for off-farm businesses such as agricultural machine maintenance within and beyond the industrial area, fostering collaboration and support between urban industrial centers and the rural agricultural sector. This not only empowers MSMEs to attain self-sufficiency and profitability but also strengthens the ties between urban and rural communities, facilitating economic recovery in both regions and contributing to the establishment of a more sustainable local economy in the long run.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="80" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="35"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
